| The script VM ran its two shift opcodes as each other -- `BSHL` performed `>>` and `BSHR` performed `<<` -- so every `<<` in a game script right-shifted. `GLYPH_VALUE` packs a colour with `colour << 12`, so every script-created field lost its colour and `src/Light.cpp` scanned it as a black light source; `(1 << 12) - 1` masks became `-1` and matched everything, which left Hallucinatory Terrain's floor test permanently false. Pure arithmetic, no dependence on integer width, the typedefs or the compiler, so Win32/MSVC misbehaves identically; both halves date from the import commit 7b8504a. The Rect member codegen (`src/RComp.cpp:1478,1510,1526`) was written against the inversion and is self-consistent with it, so it swaps in the same change -- correcting the VM alone breaks Rect member access in five live spells while every light check still passes. Two script sites that exploited the inversion flip to `>>` (`lib/pspells.irh`, `lib/wspells.irh`) (`src/VMachine.cpp`, `src/RComp.cpp`) | **Observed** -- a summoned fire elemental's `FI_LIGHT` field saved `Image=324` where the script asks for `324 \| (4 << 12)` = 16708, and the light probe scanned it as `S 112 110 2 0 0 0 3 21`, colour 0,0,0, with every surrounding cell unlit; after the fix the same fixture gives `Image=16708`, `S 112 110 2 128 0 0 3 21`, and a lit disc. A 1,836-turn seeded dive is byte-identical on both builds | no | inc-gv1u |
