| Every god's attention was paced by `xpTicks`, which counts how many TIMES the character gained XP (`src/Create.cpp`, incremented inside `GainXP`). It is neither a clock nor an amount, so a follower who stopped earning XP stopped hearing from his god, permanently. The blessing half of that is arguable pacing; the anger half is not, because retribution pauses the moment the follower stops advancing and never resumes, and a character can park indefinitely with a favour debt while nothing arrives. A god may now declare `GODPULSE_TURNS` or `GODANGER_TURNS` and be paced by the game turn instead, reusing the `lastPulse[]` slot it already owns so no member is added to `Character` and no save format moves; any mechanism may raise a request tagged with a `GPR_*` reason through `Character::RequestGodPulse`, which the existing per-god interval still throttles and the existing `HUNG_PULSE` stati still defers; and a stamp caught ahead of its own clock is repaired in place instead of silencing the god for ever. A god declaring neither constant is paced by `xpTicks` exactly as before. Upstream's, not the port's: the gate is one integer comparison between two plain members, with no typedef, pointer width, endianness or compiler extension in it, so the original Win32/MSVC build starves a parked follower identically (`src/Creature.cpp`) (renamed `GODPULSE_ROUNDS`/`GODANGER_ROUNDS` and made an exact schedule by inc-pu6v.51) | **Observed** -- `tools/check_god_pulse_request.sh`, seed 1, `tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat`, driving two synthetic gods spliced into a scratch module. Four assertions, each proved red by its own mutation and then green: reason 0 survives the periodic path (3 deliveries, every reason 0; red when the periodic path passes `GPR_REST` instead); the throttle holds under a request raised every round (6 deliveries, every gap >= 300 turns; red with the due-check disabled -- 11 deliveries, gaps down to 60 turns); a god declaring `GODANGER_TURNS` delivers 6 anger pulses to a follower who gains ZERO xpTicks (red when `byTurns` is forced false -- 0 deliveries in the whole session); and a god declaring neither constant is paced by ticks (3 deliveries, `clock=ticks` throughout, every gap >= 20 xpTicks; red when `byTurns` is forced true). The pantheon control is a whole-session A/B on `tools/keys/explore.keys` seed 1, 37,927 game turns over 1,267 keys, between a build at the epic branch's base commit and this one: the 9 rendered screens are byte-identical, and `session.log`, `mapaudit.log` and `saveprobe.log` differ only in their timestamp headers and one heap address. No shipped god declares either new constant, so that A/B measures the entire pantheon on the path this change touches | no | inc-pu6v.24 |
