| `Character::XPPenalty` charged the multiclass experience penalty by the wrong rule and at the wrong number. It asked whether the character's HIGHEST class was one his race favours and took a flat 25% when it was not, so a favoured class that was not the highest counted for nothing -- the Player's Handbook's own dwarf Fighter 7 / Cleric 2, which is meant to cost nothing, paid -- and a prestige class carrying `CF_FAVOURED`, the flag that says the class counts as favoured for everybody, was honoured only while it was also the highest, which its own entry requirements make impossible; so every prestige character paid from the level he entered the class. The manual said 20% while the code took 25%. Rewritten to the rule Brian ruled on: every class the race favours leaves the comparison, and so does every prestige class, then each remaining class standing two or more levels below the highest remaining class costs 20% and those costs add. Removing ALL of the race's favoured classes rather than the single one D&D grants is his ruling, on the grounds that D&D assumes a party and Incursion sends the player in alone. `lib/help.irh` rewritten to state the rule it now follows (`src/Create.cpp`, `lib/help.irh`) | **Observed** -- seed 1, one function between the two builds, every figure read off a character sheet (`src/Sheet.cpp:105-110`). Elf Barbarian 3 / Rogue 1 25% -> 20%; the same character with Warrior 1 added 25% -> 40%, the figure the old flat penalty could not produce at all; at Barbarian 3 / Rogue 2 / Warrior 2 25% -> nothing; Elf Rogue 5 / Assassin 2 25% -> nothing; Wood Elf Rogue 2 / Warrior 1 25% -> nothing. Control, a single-classed Elf Barbarian 3: nothing on both sides. `tools/check_xp_penalty_rule.sh`, confirmed green on the fixed build and red on the pre-fix binary, where five of the six characters fail and the control passes | no | inc-by8 |
| The Monk's `Ability[CA_KI_STRIKE]` grant was commented out in `lib/classes.irh:1404`, and no other class, race or item grants the ability, so nothing in the compiled module carried it. `src/Fight.cpp:6494-6497` is the ONLY route by which an unarmed attacker may damage an incorporeal creature -- every other arm of that gate wants an `Item` with a plus, a blessing or ghost touch -- so every monk's fist, and every claw and bite, passed clean through a ghost, wraith or shadow forever. Restored the grant line (`lib/classes.irh`). Ki Strike is damage reduction only: the ability is read at exactly two engine sites, that incorporeal gate and the branch at `src/Fight.cpp:8429-8437`, commented out at the time and since restored by inc-bei, with `src/Help.cpp:3276` and `src/Sheet.cpp:614` display-only, so restoring it adds no damage, no element and no to-hit. The bead's second claimed consequence, that `FT_WARCRY` is unreachable, is WRONG and was corrected on it: `src/FeatTab.cpp:1585-1588` gives the feat two alternative disjuncts and the first is Charisma 13 plus `FT_IMPROVED_DEMORALIZE` | **Observed** -- seed 1, one line of module data between the two builds, read off the character sheet's Special Abilities block. A Monk 4 showed no Ki Strike at all before and reads `Ki Strike +1` after; the same character at Monk 1 shows nothing on both sides, which is the grant's own "starting at 4th". `tools/check_ki_strike_live.sh`, confirmed red on the pre-fix module and green on the rebuilt one | no | inc-qep |
| `Creature::Damage` holds the ONLY test of `CA_WEAPON_IMMUNITY` in the engine, and it was gated on a hand-written list of seven attack types -- `A_SWNG`, `A_FIRE`, `A_HURL`, `A_GREA`, `A_LUNG`, `A_CALL`, `A_PREC`. `A_PUNC` (1), `A_CLAW` (6), `A_BITE` (7) and every other natural attack were absent, so a monk's fist and a housecat's claw never met the rule at all -- not beaten, never asked -- while `src/Help.cpp:3295` told the player the creature "is unaffected by weapons with a plus less than %d". The list was missing half of its own category too: `A_THRU`, `A_CHAR`, `A_RIPO`, `A_WHIR` and `A_SPRI` are manoeuvres made with the weapon in hand and bypassed the rule as well. Replaced the list with `isBlowStruckByACreature()`, a RANGE test over the `is_standard_attk` / `is_postgrab_attk` / `is_maneuver` macros `inc/Defines.h:1170-1235` already defines beside the attack constants, so a natural attack or manoeuvre added later is caught by the act that adds it; `A_HURL` is named individually only because its constant sits in the special band, and `A_COUP` is excluded on purpose (Brian ruled on 2026-08-21 that a coup de grace bypassing weapon immunity is intended). Restored the commented-out `CA_KI_STRIKE` branch three lines inside the same block at the same time -- it could never have fired even uncommented, because `A_PUNC` never reached the block. Spells, monster ability attacks and response effects fall outside every range tested; traps and acts of god arrive with `AType` 0 (nothing outside `src/Fight.cpp` assigns `EventInfo::AType`) and are also excluded explicitly (`src/Fight.cpp`) | **Observed** -- seed 1, one file between the two builds, one wizard-mode-summoned lemure (CR 1 devil, `ABILITY(CA_WEAPON_IMMUNITY,1)`, `lib/mon4.irh:1221-1229`) punched bare-handed by the same character at two levels. Pre-fix: the Monk 1 punch reads *"Catching it off-guard, you punch, hitting the lemure"* with no failure line, and the Monk 4 punch kills it. Post-fix: the Monk 1 punch read