| The whole two-weapon rule in `Creature::CalcValues` was gated on two `Item` pointers. Fists are not Items, so both are NULL bare-handed and every clause was dead -- including Two-Weapon Tempest, +10 speed and the largest two-weapon payoff in the game. `Character::HasFeat` grants a monk Two-Weapon Style for the express purpose of letting him BUY Tempest (its gate is Two-Weapon Style plus melee BAB 9), so the monk qualified, could spend a feat slot, and got nothing: he had to put his fists away and pick up two nunchaku to use the feat his fists had earned him. The SRD settles it -- "an unarmed strike is always considered a light weapon" -- so the gate now admits two empty fists. Three things had to come with it. (1) With both pointers NULL `offhandWep == meleeWep` is TRUE, so a bare-handed Double Weapon Fighting holder would have read as wielding a double weapon; the test now asks whether one ITEM fills both hands. (2) The size clause dereferences both pointers and asks whether the off hand is light; a fist is light by the SRD, so two fists skip it on the merits rather than by NULL-guard. (3) The off-hand attributes are built for a WEAPON -- `A_HIT_OFFHAND` takes its base from `AttkVal[S_MELEE]`, and a monk attacks at 75% in melee against 100% brawling -- so when the off hand is a fist the whole off-hand `AttrAdj` row is copied from the brawl row, bonus type by bonus type, before the two-weapon adjustments go on top, and the second fist in the brawl loop reads it. That replaces inc-dzz's two hand-written exemptions, which skipped the secondary-natural-attack penalties whenever both hands were empty without ever asking whether the character held the feats -- so a creature with two fists and neither feat got their benefit free. The duplicated dual-wield timing the bead's third consequence names is gone too: `WAttack` and the brawl path both call one `DualWieldTimeout()` the comment at `src/Fight.cpp:3551-3553` records it (`src/Values.cpp`, `src/Fight.cpp`, `src/Term.cpp`) | **Observed** -- seed 1, `tools/keys/monk-tempest.keys`, a Lizardfolk Monk 1 / Warrior 10 with empty hands, every figure read off the character sheet's Brawl row. Pre-fix, after buying Two-Weapon Tempest: `Speed 125% (base 100% +25% Warrior)`. Post-fix: `Speed 175% (base 100% +25% Warrior +50% dual-weapon)`. A warrior's own speed does not move between Warrior 9 and Warrior 10, so the whole 50 points is the feat. No regression on inc-dzz: the 1st-level sidebar reads `Hit:5 / 5`, `Punch:1d6+4` twice, `Spd:100%` byte-for-byte on both builds. `tools/check_two_fist_feats_live.sh`, confirmed red on the pre-fix binary and green on the fixed one. The other half of the rule -- that a two-fist fighter WITHOUT the feats now pays the ordinary penalties -- cannot be built in the game, because `src/Create.cpp` grants Two-Weapon Style and Ambidexterity to anyone with `CA_UNARMED_STRIKE` and `TwoFistFighting()` requires `CA_UNARMED_STRIKE`; it was measured instead on two probe builds differing only in that grant being compiled out. Old code, no grant: `Hit:5 / 5`, unchanged, because the exemption never read a feat. New code, no grant: `Hit:3 / 1` -- the main fist -2 for want of Two-Weapon Style and the off fist -4 for want of both, which is exactly what two daggers cost | no | inc-nie |
