| `Map::GetOpenXY` returned `0` when `OpenC` was zero, and the `ASSERT` guarding that return only calls `Error()` (`inc/Defines.h:100-101`), which logs and returns, so the return ran anyway. `0` decodes as x=0, y=0 -- a real square, in the map's always-solid outer edge -- and `Thing::PlaceOpen` passed it straight to `PlaceAt` with no test. `src/Display.cpp` relocates only creatures, so an item or a feature stayed in the rock, linked into `At(0,0).Contents`, and persisted into the save; `src/MapAudit.cpp` never tests solidity, so the audit reported clean. This is the same shape as the `Map::At` out-of-bounds defect this fork already sent as rmtew#40/#41: a query with no valid answer returns the corner square, so a wrong answer is indistinguishable from a real one. Upstream's source is unchanged at both sites -- `src/MakeLev.cpp:3385-3393` and the untested `PlaceOpen` at `inc/Map.h:723-725` on `upstream/master` -- and the logic is plain control flow with no dependence on integer width, the typedefs or the compiler, so Win32/MSVC places the same Thing in the same rock. One difference is the port's, and it is not the defect: upstream's `Error()` raises an `[E]xit or [C]ontinue?` box and returns to the caller on Continue, where the headless `Error()` returns with no prompt, so the wrong placement is silent here and follows a keypress there. Added the `NO_OPEN_XY` (`0xFFFF`) sentinel, which cannot collide with a real square on any map the shipped module declares, and `PlaceOpen` now drops the Thing with `Remove(true)` -- the idiom four generation sites in the same file already use when `RANDOM_OPEN_NEAR_SOLID` finds nothing, each on a Thing that was never placed: `src/MakeLev.cpp:3608-3611`, `:3618-3621`, `:3627-3630` and `:3637-3640` (`inc/Map.h`, `src/MakeLev.cpp`) | **Observed** -- A/B over seeds 1000-1039 of `tools/keys/explore.keys` under `tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat`, two binaries differing only in `-DINCURSION_OPENXY_UNGUARDED`, against one frozen `mod/Incursion.Mod` (md5 `c4f199bd`). One refusal happens in the 40 seeds, on seed 1025, and the Thing that follows it is what moved: before, `stranded=1` -- the Thing is found by walking `At(0,0).Contents` -- and `disposed=0`; after, `stranded=0` and `disposed=1`. Seed 1025's `logs/errors.log` carries `ASSERT failed: 'OpenC' in file src/MakeLev.cpp, line 3590` before (3590 is the line in the unfixed tree at HEAD; the `UNGUARDED` build reports 3598, where the `#ifdef` moved it) and is EMPTY after, with the map audit armed and clean. The control is the successful placements, which must not move: 376 of them over the 27 seeds that place anything, equal in total AND seed by seed on both builds. Nothing else moved either -- all 40 seeds match on exit code, turn count, key count and ending, 1426776 turns in total on each side and 39369 turns over 1267 keys on seed 1025 either way. `tools/check_open_xy.sh` is exit 1 on the `UNGUARDED` binary and exit 0 on the fixed one, and it was mutation-proved on 2026-09-09 against four rewrites of the fix that a grep cannot tell apart: `PlaceAt(_m,0,0)` behind the sentinel test (the hole its own previous version had), `Remove(false)` for `Remove(true)`, a sentinel that decodes to a real square (`0x4040`), and a transposed decode `PlaceAt(_m,xy/256,xy%256)`. All four go red. The probe those numbers come from is inert: with `INCURSION_OPENXY_PROBE` unset, and again with it set to 1, its binary produces screen dumps byte-identical to a build with no probe compiled in, on all 40 seeds. NOT CLAIMED: which object is lost. That it is the Armoury's forge -- `it = CreateFeature($"forge"); it->PlaceOpen(EMap);` in Region `"Armoury"`'s `EV_BIRTH` in `lib/dungeon.irh`, the only `PlaceOpen` in the script library not guarded by a true `FindOpenAreas` -- is **Traced** from reading its five guarded siblings in the regions `"Dragon Cave"`, `"Kobold Warren"`, `"Armoury"` and `"Ancient Library"` (twice), and is carried as inc-upw.55. Those sites are named by region and not by line because `lib/dungeon.irh` moved three lines under this work while it was being written. `PlaceOpen` is a `system` call resolved in the engine (`lib/dispatch.h:728-730`), so no module rebuild is needed; the one script that reads `GetOpenXY`'s value itself, `lib/pspells.irh:2403`, sits in the else arm of a true `FindOpenAreas` and never sees the sentinel | no | inc-upw.3 |
