he check's own run) grants all nine maladies with `GainPermStati` inside `EV_BLESSING`, once. The PLAYER then learns Heal in wizard mode and casts it on himself; no `ThrowEff` is involved, which matters because `ThrowEff` sets only `eID` and never `e.EMagic` (`src/Event.cpp:621-634`) and so cannot drive this spell at all. Fixed build: control missing none, after still present none. Mutated build, the same run with the ten `and EA_HEALING` lines deleted from a scratch copy: control missing none, after still present `BLIND CONFUSED DISEASED STUNNED POISONED HALLU BLEEDING CHOKING WOUNDED`. The identical CONTROL on both builds is the control proper -- a run in which the afflictions never landed would show an empty "after" line too, and would pass a check that read only the second line. The mutation counts what it deletes and exits 2 unless it removed exactly ten, so it cannot silently match nothing. Two things were learned building it: the right-hand status panel is a priority chain that shows at most ONE malady and never shows `HALLU`, `BLEEDING`, `CHOKING` or `WOUNDED` (`src/Term.cpp:426-444`), so the check reads the wizard "Examine Player Data" dump instead; and a stati granted with the default `eID` of 0 crashes the poison and disease ticks, filed as `inc-s5w8` | no | inc-xr8i |
