| `Armour::PenaltyVal` had two paths (`src/Item.cpp:2273`). Body armour returned the item's own authored `Penalty:`. A shield never read its `Penalty:` at all: it walked a ladder of size comparisons, so every shield of a size cost the same, the data had no say in what a shield costs, and the ladder's `-10` rung was dead code because the next line repeated the test that selected `-10` and doubled it. No shield in `lib/weapons.irh` authored a `Penalty:`, which is why the field was never missed. This is plain integer control flow over authored data: the ladder arrived in the import and misbehaves identically on Win32 with the original typedefs and compiler. Authored `Penalty:` on all six shields, made the `T_SHIELD` path read it, and replaced the ladder with one size step -- the authored figure states what a Medium bearer pays, and a bearer one size away doubles or halves it, two steps at most. A shield with no authored figure still falls back to the same ladder, so no shield can silently become free. The `+2 for_skills` softening no longer applies to shields, because it exists to absorb body armour being authored two worse than the figure it must show -- full plate is `-8` in the data and `-6` on the sheet, the SRD number -- and a shield now authors the shown figure itself (`src/Item.cpp`, `lib/weapons.irh`) | **Observed** -- `tools/check_shield_penalty.sh`, seed 4, `tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat`. Subject is the seed's own Medium paladin, who is shield-proficient through his Grants block, so no non-proficiency penalty is mixed in. Each shield is put in the Ready Hand one at a time and read twice from the character dump the sheet's `[W]` command writes: the Skill Ratings armour term and the Movement Rate shield factor, which are separate consumers of the same call (`src/Create.cpp:5702`, `src/Values.cpp:939`). After: buckler `-1` and no movement factor, small shield `-2` and `95%`, kite shield `-4` and `90%`, tower shield `-10` and `75%`. Proved red by stashing the change and rebuilding both the binary and the module: exit 1, buckler with no armour term at all, kite `-6` and `85%`, tower `-18` and `55%` -- the same figures the bead measured on 2026-09-08. The size step is read separately, on a halfling warrior at the same seed, and is Observed too: the buckler leaves `95%` and the small shield `90%`, exactly double the figures the same two shields cost the Medium paladin. The kite and tower shields are not read there because the game will not put either in a Small hand. A bearer LARGER than Medium, who halves the figures instead, stays **Traced**: no playable race is one | no | inc-rsps |
