| Three faults in `Character::Pray`/`Character::Insight`/`Character::GrantSymbol` (`src/Prayer.cpp`) all trace to a discarded `EvReturn`. (1) The trouble-aid loop's `ReThrow(EV_GIVE_AID,e)` ignored ABORT -- the engine's documented way for a god resource to decline an aid, since `ThrowEvent` (`src/Event.cpp:290-298`) returns the resource's own DONE/ABORT before ever reaching the engine's default `Character::GiveAid`, which always returns DONE -- so a god that declined was still journalled "\<Res\> aided you by \<Str\>." and still charged. (2) `GrantSymbol` returned void, so `if (Timeout) doneSomething = true` (true unconditionally, because `Timeout += 30` runs first) made the no-aid branch ("\<Res\> had no aid to give you.") unreachable and charged PrayerTimeout/INTERVENTION_COST on every prayer that passed its skill check, aid or not. (3) `Character::Insight`'s own `ReThrow(EV_GIVE_AID,e)` for AID_IDENTIFY discarded the same ABORT after already charging the insight PrayerTimeout/FavPenalty, leaving a declined insight charged same as a granted one. All three are byte-identical to the original 0.6.9H3 source (cea33d8: `ReThrow` at `src/Prayer.cpp:303` and `:1115`, `Timeout += 30`/`if (Timeout)` at `:1039`/`:1100-1101`), pure event-return and integer logic with no typedef, pointer-width or platform dependence, so Win32 misbehaves identically. Fixes: capture the trouble-loop and insight ReThrow returns and skip the journal/charge (insight: save and restore PrayerTimeout/FavPenalty) on ABORT; `GrantSymbol` now returns bool, true only when it created a symbol, and `Character::Pray` sets `doneSomething` from that instead of the deleted `if (Timeout)` test. No god shipped in `lib/religion.irh` returns ABORT from EV_GIVE_AID today, so faults (1) and (3) are LATENT in stock content (`src/Prayer.cpp`, `inc/Creature.h`) | **Observed** for faults (1) and (2); **Traced** for fault (3). `tools/check_aid_decline.sh`, seed 5, `tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat`, two binaries differing only by `-DINCURSION_AID_DECLINE_UNFIXED`. Fault (2): `tools/keys/aid-decline.keys` prays four times with nothing wrong; unfixed, the no-aid line never appears and the second prayer reads "You called for aid too soon after your last prayer."; fixed, "\<God\> had no aid to give you." appears every time and "too soon" never does -- a no-aid prayer now sets no PrayerTimeout. Fault (1): since no shipped god declines, the check builds one (`tools/fixtures/aid-decline-god.irh`, a god whose `On Event EV_GIVE_AID` returns ABORT and wounds its own follower on joining so it carries a real trouble) into a scratch module -- symlinked copies of every tracked `lib/*.irh` plus a private `main.irc`/`../inc`, compiled by the binary under test and loaded from a private run directory's `mod/`, nothing tracked touched. `tools/keys/aid-decline-god.keys` joins it and prays four times: unfixed, "Decline Aid God aided you by healing you." appears; fixed, "Decline Aid God had no aid to give you." appears in its place and "aided you by" never does. Fault (3) was traced by reading the `savedTimeout`/`savedPenalty` capture-and-restore, not exercised: `Character::Insight` gates its whole body behind an unrelated hardcoded `SkillCheck(SK_KNOW_THEO,15,true)` with its own retry cooldown, and its oracle would be a numeric Pen delta on the character sheet rather than a string a screen does or does not carry -- investigated and judged impractical for this check | no | inc-pu6v.44 |
